<header class="page-header">
  <h1>Research</h1>
  <p class="lead">Alongside the artworks I build systems that collect, verify and interpret images of the world: where a picture was taken, when, by whom, and whether independent sources agree. Much of this work is proprietary, so this page sets out the areas I work in and points to what is public.</p>
</header>

<a class="feature" href="/work/collective-memory/">
  <img src="/media/collective-memory/coverage.webp" alt="World map of the Collective Memory corpus, with clips from 174 countries" loading="eager">
  <div>
    <p class="kicker">Co-founder · Research &amp; development</p>
    <h2>Collective Memory</h2>
    <p>A distributed, contributor-led archive of geolocated observation: more than 18 million clips from 174 countries, including sustained documentation in Gaza and Ukraine. I lead research and development, from field capture to ethically sourced datasets with contributor remuneration.</p>
