  </div>
</a>

<section aria-labelledby="areas">
  <h2 id="areas" class="section-label">Areas</h2>
  <dl class="areas">
    <div>
      <dt>Verification and provenance</dt>
      <dd>Capture-time metadata, integrity checks, confirming observations against independent footage of the same place; tracing how images travel and are reused online.</dd>
      <dd class="refs"><a href="/work/collective-memory/">Collective Memory</a> <a href="/work/culvert/">Wiki Culverts</a></dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Geolocation and 3D reconstruction</dt>
      <dd>Placing imagery from pixels when GPS is missing or wrong; structure-from-motion and photogrammetry from uncalibrated and archival photographs.</dd>
      <dd class="refs"><a href="/work/collective-memory/">Collective Memory</a> <a href="/work/archive-photogrammetry/">Archival Photogrammetry</a></dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Satellite and geospatial data</dt>
      <dd>Satellite and generative remote-sensing imagery, OpenStreetMap tiles, Google Earth Engine, LiDAR, GeoJSON, and digitized historical maps.</dd>
      <dd class="refs"><a href="/work/satellite-image-exchange/">Satellite Image Exchange</a> <a href="/work/meandering-rio-commons/">Meandering Rio Commons</a> <a href="/work/lidar-shoreline/">LiDaR ShoreLINE</a> <a href="/work/dem-film/">DEM film</a></dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Computer vision on open sources</dt>
      <dd>Detection and tracking on public livestreams; face and licence-plate de-identification across photo and video at dataset scale.</dd>
      <dd class="refs"><a href="/work/bovine-weather-model/">Bovine Weather Model</a> <a href="/work/collective-memory/">Collective Memory</a></dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>AI, misinformation and on-chain data</dt>
      <dd>LLM assistants reasoning over networks of news sources; how AI inherits bias from its sources; smart contracts, subgraph indexing and brute-force key search on Ethereum.</dd>
      <dd class="refs"><a href="/work/news-currencies/">News Currencies</a> <a href="/work/searching-for-null/">Searching for Null</a></dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Fieldwork and ethnography</dt>
      <dd>Field surveys, interviews and documentation — from 1,200 culverts in Vermont to the US–Mexico border and COP26; capture tools designed for contributors documenting their own surroundings.</dd>
      <dd class="refs"><a href="/work/collective-memory/">Collective Memory</a> <a href="/work/culvert/">Wiki Culverts</a> <a href="/work/meandering-rio-commons/">Meandering Rio Commons</a> <a href="/work/into-the-oceanic/">Into the Oceanic</a></dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Sound and sensing</dt>
      <dd>Field recording, sound design and original scores; sensor-driven and robotic systems; listening as a way of documenting a place alongside the image.</dd>
      <dd class="refs"><a href="/work/the-cavalry/">The Cavalry</a> <a href="/work/dem-film/">DEM film</a> <a href="/work/cyano-bot/">Cyano-Bot</a></dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Data economics and ethical ground truth</dt>
      <dd>Consent, provenance and contributor remuneration in the production of training data; markets, tokens and prediction as objects of critique.</dd>
      <dd class="refs"><a href="/work/collective-memory/">Collective Memory</a> <a href="/work/bovine-weather-model/">Bovine Weather Model</a> <a href="/work/searching-for-null/">Searching for Null</a></dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</section>

